  That "() Defensive response" is what's killing your characters.

  Don't hit Energy Vortices with a melee weapon, you'll get shocked
every time.  (Shock resistance negates this, of course.)  Especially if
you've been engulfed by the vortex, because then you can't miss.

  
  Throw your missile weapons instead: daggers, knives, boomerang, darts,
shuriken, arrows (w/wielded bow), crossbow bolts(w/wielded crossbow),
rocks, worthless glass, valuable gems, javelins, spears, spare
warhammers, aklys, or any other weapon you may be carrying around.
(HINT: Worthless glass isn't.)  Spells are also a good alternative.
Even spare wielded weapons will work when thrown.  (The negative to-hit
modifier for thrown non-missile weapons doesn't matter if you can't miss
due to being engulfed.)  From outside the vortex you can also safely use
a polearm from a distance.  (Polearms only work as "bashing" melee
weapons from within vortices.)


  Just don't melee attack with a wielded weapon. (This goes for fire
vortices as well, although oddly not ice vortices.)


  This is the situation where many Valkyries discover to their dismay
that 1) wielding Mjollnir does not convey shock resistance and 2) most
of Mjollnir's damage comes from its d24 damage against monsters that are
NOT shock resistant.  So even throwing Mjollnir would only do Str damage
bonus (not to be sneezed at if at STR: 25 = +6 dmg) + ordinary war
hammer damage: about 3.0 pts of damage, plus a possible +3 for expert
skill, plus enchantment.  

  So Mjollnir maximum averages (12 + enchantment) points of damage to
shock resistant monsters, absolute maximum of (14+ench) against small
monsters, (13+ench) against large.  At enchantment of +7, Mjollnir
averages 19 points of damage against shock resistant monsters.

  Against non-shock resistant monsters, Mjollnir adds d24 damage.
That's a flat distribution between 1 and 24, averaging to 12.5.  Note
that doing one extra point of electrical damage is just as likely as
doing 24 extra points of electrical damage.  You're at the non-existent
mercy of the PRNG.  So maximum average against non-shock resistant
monsters would be 32.5.





